  id: Biceps_brachii_muscle.L
  partName: Biceps_brachii_muscle.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The biceps brachii is a prominent muscle of the forelimb responsible for flexing
    the elbow joint and stabilizing the shoulder. It plays an essential role in lifting
    the limb and supporting body weight during movement. '
  - This muscle also helps control limb positioning and contributes to coordinated
    motion. Working together with the brachialis and other muscles, it ensures smooth
    and controlled flexion. Its dual function in both movement and stabilization
    makes it crucial for efficient locomotion and strength.
